      "username": "fjur",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
      "created_at": "2026-09-06T17:10:59.719Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Sea-Envy\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"32561\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/sea-envy/48/1849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Sea-Envy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Christopher and Adam forgot there is a character with Density Control. Guise-Cat at D6. one of the things where “normal cat” works with the powers, I have known many cats that are were heavier and lighter that you think at different times.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, Guise-Cat is a great exercise in how flexible the system can be. Aeon Girl also has Density Control at <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/3/329c72e5b8e6369e1b922b98850b5d1a68931335.png?v=12\" title=\":d8:\" class=\"emoji emoji-custom\" alt=\":d8:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\">.</p>\n<p>And just for the record, since C&amp;A were struggling to think of any Nuclear-using heroes in real life comics, the ones I had in mind while writing the question were Captain Atom and Firestorm. Curious that the only ones they could think of were Marvel.</p>",
